Subject: [PATCH 2/6] formicary: the user-bound pattern layer: per-user trails
 over the scholia's addresses, with the measured power-law fade

organs/formicary.mjs: one colony per user (own file), trails laid only on a verified use over addresses of the corpus and the scholia (doc:<sha256>[#k], lemma:<lang>:<word>), heads are marks never text, order() is a permutation of its candidates (earned, untried as given, dead), alarms forget, the user can forgetAll, marks mirror to a caller's log with the user named.
kernel/stigmergy.js and organs/trail-store.mjs: an opt-in law: "power" (weight = (1 + age s)^-1.2, the slope measured in pharos/eoql/SIG-ANSWER.md); the default stays the 7-day exponential, so nothing that runs changes.
Not built: promotion to synapses and expressways, forgetting one head, the hunt wiring.

Tests: formicary 10, stigmergy 9, trail-store 8, reading-baseline and one-door 6, all pass. Nothing pushed.

